| FR01 | Student — Booking association | Partially (Student side multiplicity requires confirmation) |
| FR02 | Booking — Equipment association with 1 at Equipment end | Yes |
| FR03 | startDate and endDate attributes in Booking class | Yes |
| FR04 | Staff Member — Booking association (reviews) | Partially (Reviewer assignment rule unconfirmed) |
| FR05 | Staff Member — Equipment association (manages availability of) | Yes |
| FR06 | Candidate status attribute in Booking class | Needs clarification (Approval workflow logic not detailed)


## Part G — Campus Workshop Registration (New Example)

### Task G5: Interpretation Statements
1. One Student can have 0..(zero or many) Registration records
2. Each Registration belongs to 1 (exactly one) Student
3. One Workshop can have 0..(zero or many) Registration records
4. Each Registration is for 1 (exactly one) Workshop


## Part H — Assessed Individual Project Application
Scenario A: Community Volunteer & Event Coordination System

### Task H1: Candidate Domain Concepts
1. Volunteer: The community member applying for event roles
2. Event: The activity organized for community coordination
3. EventRole: Specific positions/tasks within an event e.g., restricted roles requiring Garda vetting
4. Application: The formal submission made by a volunteer to join a specific role

### Task H2 & H3: Class Associations & Multiplicities
Volunteer (1) — makes — (0..*) Application
  One Volunteer can submit zero or many Applications; each Application belongs to exactly one Volunteer
Applicatio (0..*) — for — (1) EventRole
  Each Application is submitted for exactly one EventRole; an EventRole can receive zero or many Applications
EventRole (1..*) — belongs to — (1) Event
  Each Event has one or many EventRoles; an EventRole belongs to exactly one Event

### Task H4: Open Question / Assumption
Question: Can a volunteer submit multiple applications for different roles within the same event, or are they restricted to one application per event?
Target Stakeholder: Volunteer Event Coordinator / Compliance Officer
